[55.835892, "i", "cat > /home/github/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt << 'EOF'\nRepository: AgentOps-AI/agentops\nID: agentops\n\nError Analysis:\nThe test `tests/test_events.py::TestEvents::test_record_timestamp` is failing because the timestamps don't have sufficient precision.\n\nRoot Cause:\nThe `get_ISO_time()` function in `agentops/helpers.py` uses `timespec='milliseconds'` which only provides 3 decimal places of precision (e.g., '2024-05-04T02:36:17.528Z'). When an ActionEvent is instantiated, both `init_timestamp` and `end_timestamp` are set using the same default factory `get_ISO_time()`. If the event is recorded within the same millisecond it was created, both timestamps will be identical.\n\nThe test expects that after a 0.15 second sleep between event creation and recording, the timestamps should be different. However, with only millisecond precision, if both operations happen within the same millisecond, the timestamps appear identical.\n\nFix:\nIncrease timestamp precision from milliseconds to microseconds by changing `timespe"]
[55.836165, "i", "c='milliseconds'` to `timespec='microseconds'` in the `get_ISO_time()` function. This will provide 6 decimal places of precision, allowing sub-millisecond differences to be captured.\n\nFile to fix:\n- agentops/helpers.py: Update get_ISO_time() function to use microseconds precision\nEOF\n"]
[55.841029, "o", "cat > /home/github/build/failed/failed_reasons.txt << 'EOF'\r\n"]
